# Witness data for the native binary adjoint induction

The saved adapted basis proposes the flag dimensions
`0,140,141,175,176,210,211,212,352`. Integer columns encode binary vectors
in little-endian order. The original coordinate at `(i,j)` has flat index
`16*i+j`. GAP right-action rows are transposed to Lean column actions.

These definitions are candidate witnesses, not a filtration or simplicity
proof. Their exact arithmetic and native comparisons must be certified
before applying them to the literal induced representation. In particular
all off-diagonal blocks are retained, and no semisimplicity is assumed.
The small arithmetic theorems here certify only lengths and cut dimensions.

Original CFSG computation from the published `GeneratorMatrices` sparse rule;
no external matrix marking or character table is used. See the adjacent
`CertificateData/source/README.md` for reproducibility and orientation.
Source context: Guralnick--Malle I, Proposition 5.1, pp.15--16;
Aschbacher--Smith, Chapter K, printed pp.451--452 and 457.
